{"Title":"An Act to mandate flotation devices in police vehicles","BillNumber":"S1530","DocketNumber":"SD1833","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"A_G0","Name":"Adam Gomez","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/A_G0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:38:56.777"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"A_G0","Name":"Adam Gomez","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/A_G0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:38:56.7766667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1530/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Gomez, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1530) of Adam Gomez for legislation to mandate flotation devices in police vehicles.  Public Safety and Homeland Security.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 147 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting the following sections: \r\n\tSection XXXX. Local and state police officers shall be equipped with a flotation device in their on duty vehicles. Said flotation device shall be large enough and suitable for use in a water rescue. These officials shall further receive water rescue training, including, but not limited to, instruction on how to safely and properly use flotation devices in the event of a rescue. \r\n\tSECTION 2. The municipal police training committee may promulgate regulations for purposes of implementing this Act. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J22","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}